            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scratchpad/eq4/measure.sh"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "6c15fc95bd4272348610ddfe53d3a76889c37885324529bbd5a4cbe54b258758",
            "failure_scenario": "A refactor drops ci.yml lines 200-202; CI stays green and still refuses a broken table at seed time, but a passing run no longer prints the table to the job log.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "note": "scratchpad/eq4/measure.sh sha256 a9fa2e5bd2dc2637f609708b95006952bb9a38ff12830f00c52a0913a665f238. Table: clean rc=1 docker_calls=1 refusal=0 (the stub returns no RUSTUP_HOME); R6-broken rc=1 docker_calls=0 refusal=1; R6-broken+S2 rc=1 docker_calls=1 refusal=1."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "p1-not-equivalent",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Measured: P1 (drop read_pin's [ -f ] check) is NOT equivalent. For an absent file or a directory both versions exit 1 with empty stdout, and only the message differs. For a non-regular readable file (process substitution, /dev/fd/63), the original refuses it (rc 1, 'no toolchain file'), while P1 reads it and returns rc 0 with '1.93.0 '. The absent-file row (line 150) checks rc only on a missing path. A row 'read_pin <(printf ...)' expecting rc 1 would kill P1. Agreed with the author as follow-up; recorded as a survivor."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
